      "overall_rating": 0,
      "review_title": "",
      "review_description": "Asking for 3 quotes was a bit of a sham as I was already 99% certain I would get Country Solar NT to do the job.  This was due to personal recommendations from a couple of locals (which I have always valued far more than advertising campaign) and some inside information that they were getting expert advice on the technology to use.  My roof is at a 24 degree pitch and not ideal but I am in Darwin! With northeast and southwest facing surfaces the research I had done (largely through the Solar Quotes site) led me to believe that using microinverters and splitting the panels was the way to go.Two out of three of the companies that were asked to quote contacted me. Neither of them recommended splitting the panels or using microinverters even after this was suggested by me.  Without prompting Country Solar NT recommended this as an option (a bit more expensive).There were delays due to panels not being delivered to Darwin on time and the only issue was that Country Solar NT did not communicate about this until contacted.  Installation occurred over a day and they were good people and there was immediate connection to the grid without any issues. Back up has only been needed once when the Enphase Enlighten app needed reconnecting to the WiFi. Support was easily accessed and the problem solved within a day.I was happy with the price and, at the time, there was $1000 Smart Energy Grant from the NT Government. The 25 cent per kWh paid for exported power is certainly an incentive. Previous power bills were about $2000 per annum (we don't use A/C much like some). The three quarterly bills so far total $298.54 in credit.There should be more of it in Darwin!",
